ception of sales  and still try and get the best talent  into the best sales jobs in the country  and that's what we did  and we had to pivot a little bit so we  now operate in the us  um for a couple of months afterwards we  launched a webinar series which  he obviously thankfully and uh very kind  of you joined us on uh which is a great  episode but the idea of  that was still to add value to sales  people and to business owners  in what was a difficult time and and the  learn  was just don't stand still stick to your  principles stick to whatever your vision  is  um you're just in a more difficult  situation to try and get through it  that's all you know it's all the same  i love that so the next question i have  for you and i'm sure this has sort of  been things that you've been learning  and  sort of sharing with your your team and  speak to people about but what  working from home tip could you share  with other recruiters that has had a  massive impact on your own  productivity that's a really good one  i i've probably got a few actually um so  one i've used recently  um i've been wearing jeans uh that  sounds so so  simple but i've been i've been put been  putting jeans off i've got jeans on  right now i've been trying to dress  only a little bit smarter you know still  very casual and  and it just really helps with your  mindset because you feel like you're  you're getting ready for something um  and although you're probably walking  from your bedroom to another bedroom or  to your dining room  it just helps that you're breaking that  up with actually i'm putting a pair of  jeans on i'm getting ready for the day  so that that has helped me recently  actually particularly with this  lockdowns i think this one has been  a bit more challenging for people you  know the weather's not as good we've got  the sunshine like we had last time  and this has been going on for over a  year so that that's helped me  in this lockdown particular um  and i think the other thing is just make  sure you organize um  and try and have as much separation as  possible you know i've heard and seen  many reports that  people are actually working longer now  they're being at home probably making  the most of the time they would  typically spend commuting  but it's still important that you have  that separation and so if that's you  work upstairs as soon as you come  downstairs  work is done for the day i think that's  really really important  because when your home becomes your work  it's very difficult to uh  to separate the two yeah nice great tips  there  so what has been the most effective way  for you to win business in the last 12  months  great question um being creative has  probably been the best one  um and in the last 12 months with it  being you know much more challenging  less businesses recruiting and still you  know the same  typical amount of recruiters going after  the same business it's  being hyper personalized making sure  you're targeting the right people  and for the right reasons um and you  know i've said it a couple of times  already but make sure you're actually  adding value to that person you're  trying to prospect  um so there that's probably been my main  tips really so the biggest success  i had was probably back in june july  time we're just sending a really  personalized video  um to a recruitment manager at a big  cyber security business  and at the time that was the only video  of its type they had received  they were looking to hire you know a big  team of sdrs in the uk and in the usa  um and i think what really worked well  there was just the personalization  it stood out and it was different um so  that's been the most effective for me  really just doing whatever you can do  to stand out from the crowd i think is  more important now than it than it's  probably ever been before  yeah i love that just being open minded  isn't it to try different things and  yeah i love that  so what habit or hobby did you start in  2020 that you're gonna continue in 2021  wow um probably doing videos  was definitely one that was a work habit  and i think the key with that is  consistency you know you can do one  video it doesn't work it's easy to give  it up  um but just set yourself a target of  however many you want to do on a weekly  basis i think he's key  and doing it over a long period of time  the hobby um  has probably been running so we we  actually set up a work  uh running club um in the first lockdown  um  and money to get my 5k time from  probably 29 minutes to just under 23.  i've heard i've heard like that's just  made you all hate neil moore this  running club because he's just  constantly pounding the pavement mate oh  you know he is massively but he was it  was really funny though we had them  we're trying to get as many people  involved in the group as possible and  and one of the guys in london his uh his  girlfriend  uh was added to the group and and the  first run she posted i think it was was  a half marathon in  in just under two hours or two hours wow  and that beat neil's time  so the next day the next  but it was it was good to have that  camaraderie so that that for me is  you know going to be one uh my aim is to  do a marathon this year um  off the back of that um yeah so yeah  we'll see  so i so i wanna know carl like what  which do you think is better the first  coffee in the morning or the first  post work on a friday uh definitely  definitely the first time definitely the  first pine i've actually  tried to cut down on coffee a bit i'm  not sure about you but  um i think if you have too much during  the day um then i think you can end up  crashing and burning a little bit  earlier um  whereas after that first pint you're  done for the day then so you can  probably enjoy it  nice right so this one's slightly  different i just want to give you a  scenario and i'm just interested to  hear hear how you would approach it so  the scenario is  a particular business you've had on your  target client list for over a year long  period of time  during that time you've had a number of  touch points with different people in  that business they might have engaged  some of your content  you might send them a video over email  you've had different touch points  but through your candidate network you  managed to get one of the hiring  manager's contact details so you call  that person  they pick up they say hello who is this  and interested to hear how you'd  approach that  yeah um relevant question actually so um  one of the businesses we bought on i  actually did linkedin post about it  yesterday so the business that we  um recently been working where we were  with them a couple of years ago we  placed an sdr there 18 months ago  and they've now progressed into a  management role and are now  recruiting for their team and working  with us to do so and that client  was brought on in exactly the scenario  that you just mentioned  exactly the same way um so the way i  would approach it  um i would just go in look i've been  past your details by this person  now the key here is um and i've  mentioned this in my previous video  is this only works if the person that  you've been recommended into by you've  delivered an amazing experience for  previously so this only is effective  when you do that but the way i would  approach it is just go  look you know person x is recommended we  get in touch and i would talk about  their journey and their experience  the reason i believe they wanted to put  me in touch with you was based on the  experience that they had  we were able to do this for them and  look how well they're doing now in your  business  why don't we have a chat about how we  can support your sales team how's that  going for you right now  so that's probably how i would approach  that call but it only works  if you know you deliver great  experiences for people all the time if  not then obviously it could backfire a  little bit  yeah no i like that brilliant so final  question  is i want you to imagine that i'm a  recruiter or recruiters listening to  this and  they've set their goals for 2021 they're  feeling motivated they  are completely convinced they're gonna  have a better year this year than they  are  2020. and i just want to sort of hear  what your advice would be to me and the  recruiters listening  that you think would give us the best  possible chance of achieving the goals  that we've set this year  yeah um i think the first bit of advice  i would give probably taking it right  back to the beginning is make sure you  probably revisit and just check your  goals one that they're realistic but i  think the key thing is make sure  make sure you really want them you know  a goal is only as powerful as how much  you really want to achieve it  if you set a goal that you're not that  bothered to achieve the how you're going  to do it doesn't really matter  um doesn't really help but once you have  you know done that make sure your goals  are realistic  you can measure them you really want to  achieve them and then you need to start  working on  how you're going to make that a reality  and the key thing is just breaking it  down like it's really really simple  a 12 month goal you can lose focus you  can get a bit disillusioned but if you  break that 12-month goal down into well  actually every single month i just need  to do this or  even better every single week i need to  do this you know it's much more  manageable and i think you're much more  likely to achieve it but  yeah i think the key part of that  question is is the first bit i think the  goals  have to be strong enough you have to  really want them and then i think the  how  you know you need to think about that  but i think if the goals are good enough  you'll you'll do whatever it takes and  you will make them happen  so i would spend more time making sure  the goals are you know  really really strong yeah love that car  that's 15 minutes with the mentor that  was it  thank you so much no thank you  appreciate it

